transcript:
TOOL_CALL: ap_load_guide {"topic":"build_flow"}
TOOL_RESULT: "# Guide: Build an automation Load this right before you build, after discovery is done and the needed connections are selected. Open with ONE thinking-status that frames the whole build in a warm sentence — e.g. \"I'll wire up the trigger, connect the apps, and double-check it satisfies your goal be…"
ASSISTANT: Great idea — let me find the LinkedIn integration and then we can get this set up.
TOOL_CALL: ap_research_pieces {"pieceNames":"[\"linkedin\"]"}
TOOL_RESULT: null
ASSISTANT: Before I jump in — to write great LinkedIn posts every morning, I'll need a couple of things from you:
TOOL_CALL: ap_show_questions {"questions":[{"type":"choice","title":"Post content","question":"What should each morning's post be about?","options":[{"label":"AI-written post on a topic I choose","icon":"bot","description":"I pick themes/topics and AI drafts a fresh post each day"},{"label":"Pull from a content list I have","icon":"file-text","description":"I have posts pre-written (in a sheet, table, or doc)"},{"label":"Industry news & insights","icon":"globe","description":"AI reads trending topics and writes a relevant post each day"}]}]}
TOOL_RESULT: {"dismissed":true,"message":"The user skipped these questions. Proceed with reasonable defaults where possible, and let the user know what assumptions you made."}
ASSISTANT: No worries — I'll go with a smart default: AI drafts a fresh, engaging post each morning based on topics you care about. We can refine the themes after it's built.

Let me get your LinkedIn connected and start building.
TOOL_CALL: ap_show_connection_picker {"piece":"linkedin","displayName":"LinkedIn"}
TOOL_RESULT: {"dismissed":true,"message":"The user chose not to select a LinkedIn account. Do not pick one on their behalf. Ask: \"Would you like me to continue building with a placeholder you can connect later, or would you prefer to stop here?\""}
ASSISTANT: No problem! Would you like me to continue building the automation now (you can connect your LinkedIn account when you're ready to turn it on), or would you prefer to pause here?
TOOL_CALL: ap_show_quick_replies {"replies":["Build it now, I'll connect LinkedIn later","Stop here for now"]}
TOOL_RESULT: {"displayed":true}
